=== ladder top: sampling scale 4 ===
amplification board: peak additional heap and work vs each cell's model (input bytes by default; total I/O for output-dominated operations; value width for numbers). Per-unit readings show the larger cost density of the two samples.
green iff every meter's exponent <= 1.15, constants within: heap <= 1024 + 18 * units bytes, scan <= 90 bits/B, touch <= 24 touches/B; and every liveness floor met. All ceilings and floors apply at both sample sizes. Growth fits require denominator span >= x1.5; heap readings are clamped to 4096 B only for that fit. Growth below that resolution is unobserved by the fit. Small-input samples check only ceilings and floors. An unjudged exponent renders -.--. These finite checks are regression evidence, not universal resource guarantees.

liveness declarations on this board:
  heap floor: deterministic-liveness: the forked child materializes its own party bits today (fork builds both halves, not an in-place edit); a shared-buffer representation would lower this floor deliberately
  heap floor: materializes a result at least as large as its required output bytes
  heap n/a: a rejecting or empty outcome materializes no result, and buffering the fed stream is not semantically forced: allocation stays the implementation's choice
  heap n/a: decimal digits may be streamed directly: heap allocation is not required
  heap n/a: may compute in place or return word-scale results: allocation is not semantically forced (the process allocator itself cannot be re-routed around)
  heap n/a: one hole may live inline and its version buffer may be shared
  heap n/a: paths and rises may share input storage or live inline; heap allocation is not required
  heap n/a: serde transfers the caller's byte allocation into the decoded value; only validation state may allocate
  heap n/a: small numerators may remain inline: cloning need not allocate
  heap n/a: the forked child's version hand-over is a refcount bump on the shared stored buffer, never a byte copy, and no other allocation is semantically forced
  heap n/a: the representation may share the bound list and every version buffer: no allocation is semantically forced
  heap n/a: word-sized counts may use inline storage
  scan floor: may answer at the first divergence: still reads the operands' root codes
  scan floor: must examine its operands: at least one scanned bit per input byte
  scan floor: rejection by the pair relation: the fused decode parses the whole composite before pronouncing non-dominance (structural errors take precedence on multiply-defective input), so every fed byte is examined
  scan floor: rejection with the defect at the stream's end by construction: a self-delimiting stream's truncation, trailing bits, or non-canonical tail is only discoverable by parsing to it
  scan floor: the pair's one overlapping region sits at both id operands' preorder ends by construction and the encoded coding has no random access, so any correct rejection scans the id streams to it; the version operands ride unread (the party join is the rejection gate), so the floor covers the id bytes alone
  scan floor: the pair's one overlapping region sits at both operands' preorder ends by construction, and the encoded coding has no random access: any correct rejection scans to it
  scan floor: the paired tick walk examines every topology bit and payload code of both operands at least once: 8 bits per input byte, the walk's irreducible single examination
  scan floor: the reconciliation's version join must read both version streams in full to emit their union; the party leg guarantees only its root tags — the fused sum-split splices a subtree owned by one side alone without scanning its nodes, so no party-bytes floor is justified
  scan n/a: Count has no encoded stream to walk
  scan n/a: clones bound handles without reading their encoded version streams
  scan n/a: decides same-form equality on the stored canonical bytes wholesale (the compare may legitimately stop at the first differing byte): no stream walk is in the contract
  scan n/a: moves or hashes the stored canonical bytes wholesale: no stream walk is in the contract
  scan n/a: operands are decoded rank values: no encoded stream exists
  scan n/a: the canonical rank bytes are read through a plain slice walk, not the metered encoded primitives; the heap floor carries the row's liveness
  scan n/a: the forked party is the seed: its encoded form is empty
  scan n/a: the whole-interval (seed) party's projection is the version itself, handed back as a buffer-sharing clone: no stream walk is in the contract
  touch floor: deterministic-liveness: the balanced reduction's first-level merges each emit over their two inputs' common refinement — at least the larger input's nonzero-stored-delta count per byte-distinct arrival-adjacent pair, nothing for an equal pair (canonical equality answers it); later levels merge derived groups and are deliberately un-floored
  touch floor: deterministic-liveness: the fold lands every summand in the running accumulator today, at least one digit touch per summand; digit state moving to an unmetered representation lowers this floor deliberately
  touch floor: deterministic-liveness: the fused sweep lands each nonzero stored delta of either operand in the one running difference accumulator, at least one digit touch per boundary the larger nonzero-delta count's operand steps (a zero delta folds nothing, and a sign re-read where nothing folded is not forced); digit state moving to an unmetered representation lowers this floor deliberately
  touch floor: deterministic-liveness: the kernel folds each nonzero stored delta code of its version operands through the metered accumulator today, at least one digit touch per nonzero delta (a zero delta folds nothing: an accumulator add of zero is a no-op); digit state moving to an unmetered representation lowers this floor deliberately
  touch floor: deterministic-liveness: the validator's running height folds every stored payload code wider than the machine-word bound through the metered accumulator today, at least one digit touch per 64 code bits (word-scale deltas legitimately batch in the accumulator's lazy zone); digit state moving to an unmetered representation lowers this floor deliberately
  touch n/a: Count uses ordinary big-integer operations, not the skyline accumulator
  touch n/a: a tick whose party owns the whole tree raises bases in place through plain arithmetic: no delta fold is in the contract
  touch n/a: decoded rank values combine through ordinary big-integer arithmetic: no accumulator is in the contract
  touch n/a: every stored code fits the machine-word bound: word-scale deltas batch in the accumulator's lazy zone and force no digit touches
  touch n/a: id trees store no magnitudes: there is no digit state to meter
  touch n/a: magnitudes may be moved, hashed, or compared wholesale without a running fold: no accumulator work is in the contract
  touch n/a: rejection forces no accumulator fold: digit-state work may be deferred past the walk that finds the defect
  touch n/a: the empty version's tick is id-directed growth: the grow kernel runs no accumulator
  touch n/a: the fused placement walk's delta-fold count varies with how the bounds partition the probe's intervals: no per-byte fold count is forced
  touch n/a: the operand streams store no fold-forcing delta codes: there is no fold to meter
  touch n/a: the operands are byte-identical: canonical equality answers the pair before any sweep, so no accumulator fold is forced
  touch n/a: the operands are concurrent, so the comparison may decide at one witness divergence per direction: no delta-fold count is forced
  touch n/a: the projection may keep owned regions verbatim and re-base boundaries through plain arithmetic: no accumulator fold is forced
  touch n/a: the query admits the probe: one witness event outside the bound decides it, so no delta-fold count is forced
  resource models (model[...] rows): `trend` units govern the exponent fit; `constant` units govern the proportional reading; one `units` range means both axes agree. An explicit ceiling replaces only that currency's global proportional ceiling. Every model retains the global exponent bound and is printed on each row that uses it

